# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Build context exclusions.
#
#  Two jobs: keep the context small (this repo carries a few hundred MB of
#  node_modules, git history and old chart screenshots) and make it impossible
#  to bake a secret into an image layer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- secrets / credentials: never in an image layer -------------------------
# common/ is bind-mounted by docker-compose.yml, so the container gets the real
# files at runtime. Excluding the whole directory here means keys.api (bot
# token, DB password, CMC/CG/Finnhub keys) cannot end up in a pushed image even
# by accident. The two entries under it are redundant but kept as signposts.
common
common/keys.api
common/puppeteer-cache
# stuff/ is the author's scratch directory: production + test bot tokens,
# tsuki.pem, a Google Cloud key, DB backups. Never ship it.
stuff
# docker-compose reads POSTGRES_PASSWORD from .env on the host. Without these
# entries the file lands in the build context and the DB password is baked into
# an image layer, where it survives even if a later layer deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Any stray credential material that happens to be sitting in the repo root.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
keys.api

# --- installed / generated at build time ------------------------------------
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- VCS, editor and tooling ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.vs
.jshintrc
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
eslint.config.mjs
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml

# --- docs and host-only config ----------------------------------------------
# docs/ is mounted straight from the host by compose for the DB init script,
# so it does not need to be in the image.
docs
*.md
LICENSE
# pm2 ecosystem files: the container is supervised by docker's restart policy,
# not pm2.
process.json
metaProcess.json

# --- runtime output / local state -------------------------------------------
# ~55 saved chart screenshots; the container recreates
# chartscreens/generated-charts/ itself.
chartscreens
# Per-server tag data. Written and rebuilt at runtime; bind-mount it from the
# host if you want it to survive a rebuild.
tags.json

# --- images -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker matches these per path segment (unlike .gitignore), so the recursive
# form is needed. public/*.png must be re-included: express.static serves
# tsukilogo.png, bera*.png, crab*.png etc. into the chart page, and charts
# render wrong without them.
**/*.png
!public/*.png

# --- tests and one-off dev scratch scripts ----------------------------------
# The runtime image does not run the suite (node --test is a dev workflow), and
# devDependencies are omitted from node_modules anyway.
test
alertsTesting.js
scheduledactiontestinhell.js
